  "body": "Part of #3663 (the tool library dialog). Step U12: the Holders page, list and editor. After U8 (the dialog frame).\n\n## What happens\n\n![holder list: mockup left, current right](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/toollib-compare/4-holder-list.png)\n![holder editor: mockup left, current right](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/toollib-compare/5-holder-editor.png)\n\n- The list is close to the mockup, but has no New holder, Import or Export, and the filter is a bare box with a label.\n- The holder view is read-only: the values are text lines. There is no clamping range, no outline edit and no \"Used by\". The drawing is cut off.\n\n## Expected (mockup)\n\n- **List:** one header row with a search box and **New holder**, **Import**, **Export**. **Search** matches the taper, the clamp type, the bore or collet size and the name together (\"BT40 ER32\", \"shrink 12\"), shows \"N of M holders\", and Esc clears it.\n- **Editor** for a user holder (a built-in holder opens read-only, with \"Copy as user holder\" as today): Name, Taper, Clamp, **Clamps from / to**, Gauge length, Largest diameter, Nose diameter as inputs; the drawing with the spindle nose box and the shank range; **Used by** (the tools that use the holder); footer Duplicate, Cancel, Apply. Each edit is an undoable command and every tool that uses the holder derives again in the same undo step.\n- **Edit outline** and **Import STEP** can be a later step if this PR gets too large; say so in the PR.\n\n## Done means\n\n- Tests for the search; for each editable field (lands, undoes, the tools that use it change in one step); for a refusal when a value breaks a tool's fit; for the read-only built-in view.\n- Page layout tests for the list and the editor.\n- Before and after screenshots in the PR body.\n\nEffort: high (an editor with derived updates and its tests). Safety: the holder outline feeds the collision checks, so the outline stays never smaller than the steel.\n",
